NAME
    impact - the units a change can affect, with the rule and the file

SYNOPSIS
    impact [--base REV] [--head REV] [--tier T] [--depth N] [--also TERMS] [--map-age DAYS] [--inputs FILE] [--lunap-base REV] [--lunap-head REV] [--repo DIR]
    impact --explain FILE [--tier T]
    impact --base REV --head REV --blast FILE
    impact --base REV --head REV --format blast

DESCRIPTION
    A command of the emusen.testing module. It reads the files that
    differ between the merge base of --base (default WiseMan) and --head
    (default HEAD, with the working tree's uncommitted changes) and prints
    one line per unit, tab-separated:

        kind    unit    reason    via

    kind is cargo or dotnet; unit a crate folder or a test class's full
    name; reason the rule that chose it; via the file that brought it.
    The rules, in order, the first reason for a unit kept:

        recording  a changed recording (a line of kind 'recording' in
                   Testing/inputs.json) selects its owner, or, when the
                   owner is mapped by case and the map has the group the
                   recording's name keys (Main-1280x800.spec to
                   Owner#Main), that group alone; a file ending as a
                   recording does (.spec, .golden, ...) that no line owns
                   selects the tier's whole set
        always     a test class's own file selects the class; a unit that
                   failed in this branch's last trial is selected again
        declared   a folder line of Testing/inputs.json matching the file
                   adds its units and narrows a reached test project to
                   them; a line on another crate the closure reaches adds
                   its units, and such lines narrow only when every crate
                   through which the closure enters C# (an edge to a
                   project or an MSBuild file) has one. An entry covered:PATHSPEC
                   adds the classes the coverage map saw execute the files
                   the pathspec names (a Rust crate's C# surface, which
                   coverlet cannot see from the Rust side), and without a
                   map adds nothing and narrows nothing. For a covered
                   file only a line's cargo: and lunap entries apply
        covered    a changed .cs file the coverage map has seen selects
                   the classes that executed it (`man coverage`), plus
                   every class the map has no report for. A .cs file the
                   change adds selects the classes that executed the
                   changed files the map has seen that name its types,
                   directly or through other added files; an added file
                   nothing names, a file never executed, or a file that
                   is not C# falls to the rules below. A unit CLASS#KEY
                   is one group of a class's cases, mapped by case, run
                   by its display name
        graph      the file's owner (its nearest crate or project, or the
                   project that imports it) and everything in its reverse
                   closure over Cargo path dependencies, workspaces,
                   ProjectReference and Import, and the host's crate edges
                   (the parts of xtask/libraries.tsv); a test project the
                   closure reaches and no line narrows is selected whole
        closed     a file no rule claims selects the tier's whole set:
                   unknown is closed, never open

    A line of kind 'none' (documentation, ignore lists, CI files) claims a
    file and selects nothing. A tier's named_only classes (WindowFitAudit-
    Tests at land) are selected only by a line naming them, or by the
    covered rule when they executed the file; its excluded tags (nightly)
    are left out. --depth limits the reverse closure, as the fast tier
    does with 1. --also TERMS adds the classes the |-separated filter
    terms name, with the reason 'given'. --inputs FILE reads the lines
    from that file instead of the head revision's Testing/inputs.json,
    to try a line before committing it or to replay history with
    today's lines.

    The toolkit's own changes can count too: with --lunap-base REV the
    sibling LunaP checkout that LunaP.props names is diffed from REV to
    --lunap-head (default HEAD, with its uncommitted changes), and each
    file enters as lunap:<path>, which the map records the toolkit's
    files under: a file the map has seen selects the units that
    executed it, and one it has never seen closes to the tier's whole
    set, never to nothing. The count is said on standard error. Off by
    default (none): held on 2026-11-03 while LunaP's move into this
    repository is decided, which would make the sibling diff
    unnecessary.

    The map is used when its revision is at most --map-age days (default
    1) older than the merge base of --base and --head; an older map, or
    none, is said on standard error and the covered rule is off, so the
    graph answers as before. The map is rebuilt by the nightly.

    --format blast prints the selection as blast.sh prints its answer:
    'dotnet filter: ' with a FullyQualifiedName~ term per class and the
    tier's exclusion, 'cargo: ' per crate, 'lunap: selected', and
    'closed: FILE' for each file that fell to the closed rule, which is
    where land.sh lets blast.sh's map answer instead.

    --explain FILE prints the file's owner, what its closure reaches, the
    lines it matches and its selection. --blast FILE compares the
    selection with what blast.sh printed for the same revisions: each
    unit as 'agree', 'impact' (impact only) or 'blast' (blast.sh only),
    blast.sh's filter terms resolved to classes under its own exclusions,
    its unmapped files, and a summary line. land.sh logs this while the
    two run side by side.

    Terms that name no class are reported on standard error. See
    EmuSen_Testing.md §3.2 and §6.

EXAMPLES
    impact
    impact --base WiseMan --head approve-fix --tier land
    impact | grep -c '^dotnet'
    impact --explain EmuSen.Mistress/Views/CoresWindow.axaml.cs
    impact --base f1592d39e^1 --head f1592d39e^2 --blast blast.txt | grep -v ^agree
    impact --base WiseMan --head pausecard --format blast | sed -n 's/^dotnet filter: //p'
